## Runtime dependencies with a license other than Apache 2.0

| Component | License | How it is used |
|---|---|---|
| KiCad 10.0.4 | GPL-3.0-or-later | External application. kicad-mcp talks to a running KiCad instance over its local IPC socket (`kicad-python`) and invokes `kicad-cli` as a subprocess. KiCad itself is neither modified, embedded, nor redistributed. |
| `pcbnew` (KiCad's SWIG Python bindings) | GPL-3.0-or-later | Invoked as short-lived `python3 -c "..."` subprocesses against the **system** Python that ships with KiCad — never imported into this project's virtual environment or shipped with it (see `src/kicad_mcp/bridge/autoroute.py`). |
| Freerouting 2.1.0 | GPL-3.0-or-later | Invoked as a separate headless JVM subprocess (a `.jar` supplied by the user via `KICAD_MCP_FREEROUTING_JAR`) to autoroute a board. Not linked into kicad-mcp; communicates via files on disk (DSN/SES). |
| `kicad-skip` | LGPL-2.1-or-later | Regular pip dependency (declared in `pyproject.toml`), imported dynamically to edit `.kicad_sch` files directly (KiCad 10 does not expose schematic editing over IPC). Unmodified, used as an ordinary library. |
| `kicad-python` | MIT | Regular pip dependency. IPC client library for the KiCad API. |
| `mcp` (Model Context Protocol SDK) | MIT | Regular pip dependency. |
| `pydantic` | MIT | Regular pip dependency. |
| `protobuf` (transitive, via `kicad-python`) | BSD-3-Clause | Transitive dependency, unmodified. |

## Why this doesn't create a licensing conflict

Apache 2.0 code invoking GPL/LGPL programs as **separate processes**
(subprocess + IPC/socket, files on disk) — rather than linking against
their code or redistributing them — is the standard pattern used
throughout the KiCad automation ecosystem, and does not place this
project's own source under GPL. KiCad, `pcbnew`, and Freerouting are
never vendored, statically or dynamically linked, or shipped as part
of a kicad-mcp release; a user must install/provide them separately.
This note is descriptive, not legal advice — see `docs/BACKLOG.md` and
`CLAUDE.md` frontera F5 for the project's policy on adding dependencies.

